Since several folks have asked this, I will inject my opinion.

I interpreted the original comment to mean: if you have found better
armor, it is likely that you have also gained some experience levels. 
Therefore, protection costs more. 

However, as others have pointed out, it is possible to get good armor
without gaining experience, by letting your pet do the fighting and
collecting what's left behind.  If you rely on your pet to test
cursedness of armor, then you don't even need an altar.  (Although I
find that this may take too long, if you are playing a class that does
not start with food.) 

I am usually too impatient to run the protection racket.  Waiting for my
pet to kill everything is tedious, and because of my somewhat hasty
style of play, I usually wind up getting killed in the Mines if I don't
have many HP. 

And you CAN get lots of protection late in the game, even if you reach a
pretty high experience level.  Even without Ludios, there are magic
memory vaults and a TON of loot in Gehennom.  I have usually been able
to buy protection *at least* five or six times before I go for the final
run. 

Also, given that ALL your hard-earned protection can disappear because
of one stupid mistake, I really don't find it to be all that important. 
I view it as a bonus, something to do with all that gold that I
inevitably accumulate, not as a major goal to strive for early in the
game. 

